menu "Waveshare 7 inch display"

    config BOARD_LCD_PCLK_MHZ
        int "RGB pixel clock (MHz)"
        range 10 24
        default 16
        help
            Waveshare's demo runs the panel at 16 MHz, about 40 frames a
            second. A higher clock draws more PSRAM bandwidth and makes drift
            more likely when Wi-Fi and flash are busy.

    config BOARD_LCD_BOUNCE_LINES
        int "Bounce buffer height (lines)"
        range 4 48
        default 10
        help
            Two internal-RAM bounce buffers of this many lines feed the panel,
            so it keeps streaming while PSRAM is busy. 480 must divide evenly
            by this. 10 lines is 2 x 16 KB.

    config BOARD_LVGL_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "LVGL task priority"
        default 4

    config BOARD_LVGL_TASK_STACK
        int "LVGL task stack (bytes)"
        default 8192

endmenu
